  "qbdi_limits": {
    "threads": "A QBDI VM traces only the thread that calls run/call; other threads run natively. run, call, setOptions and precacheBasicBlock are not reentrant and must not be called from a callback (QBDI 0.12.1 docs/source/api_description.rst, 'User callbacks'). Not exercised: the probe is single-threaded.",
    "signals": "VMEvent SIGNAL, SYSCALL_ENTRY, SYSCALL_EXIT and VMState.lastSignal are 'Not implemented' (QBDI 0.12.1 include/QBDI/Callback.h). A signal handler is not traced. Not exercised.",
    "exceptions": "The ExecBroker does not support any exception mechanism, including setjmp/longjmp (QBDI 0.12.1 docs/source/api_description.rst, 'Instrumentation ranges'). Not exercised.",
    "shared_process": "Host and guest share heap and libraries; non-reentrant code such as the allocator must stay outside the instrumented range (QBDI 0.12.1 docs/source/intro.rst, 'Limitations'). The declared scope holds only the probe subject.",
